#N canvas 40 60 1200 980 one-step 0;
#X text 20 10 ONE LEARNING STEP ([r \$0-step]) with the learning rate eta_\$0 and the radius rad_\$0. A [t b b ...] fires from right to left: read it from its right outlet. Weights: the arrays wx\$0 \, wy\$0. Places on the grid: gi\$0 \, gj\$0., f 165;
#X obj 420 100 t b b b b;
#X obj 420 70 r \$0-step;
#X text 540 100 <- steps 1) to 4) \, right outlet first, f 30;
#X text 20 150 1) AN EXAMPLE: a random point of the shape - one of its two rectangles (chosen in proportion to their areas) \, uniform inside it., f 52;
#X obj 420 150 t b b;
#X obj 460 176 expr br_\$0 = random(0 \, 1000000) < pa_\$0 * 1000000 \; u1_\$0 = float(random(0 \, 1000000)) / 1000000 \; u2_\$0 = float(random(0 \, 1000000)) / 1000000, f 60;
#X obj 420 242 expr xi_\$0 = if(br_\$0 \, ax_\$0 + aw_\$0 * u1_\$0 \, bx_\$0 + bw_\$0 * u1_\$0) \; yi_\$0 = if(br_\$0 \, ay_\$0 + ah_\$0 * u2_\$0 \, by_\$0 + bh_\$0 * u2_\$0), f 60;
#X text 20 300 2) COMPETITION: the unit whose weight vector is nearest to the example wins (squared distance)., f 52;
#X obj 420 300 t b b;
#X obj 480 326 expr bd_\$0 = 1e+09 \; bk_\$0 = 0;
#X obj 420 356 t b b;
#X msg 480 382 0;
#X msg 420 382 36;
#X obj 420 408 until;
#X obj 420 434 f;
#X obj 470 434 + 1;
#X obj 420 462 t f f;
#X obj 480 488 expr dd_\$0 = pow(wx\$0[\$f1] - xi_\$0 \, 2) + pow(wy\$0[\$f1] - yi_\$0 \, 2);
#X obj 420 520 expr bd_\$0 = min(dd_\$0 \, bd_\$0) \; bk_\$0 = if(dd_\$0 < bd_\$0 \, \$f1 \, bk_\$0);
#X text 800 520 <- right to left: bk_\$0 is decided with the old best distance \, then the best distance is updated. Ties: the lower unit number wins., f 34;
#X text 20 560 3) LEARNING: every unit within the radius of the winner ON THE GRID moves towards the example: w <- w + eta * (x - w). Distance on the grid = max(|row difference| \, |column difference|) \, a square neighbourhood (Rojas \, Algorithm 15.2.1). Radius 0: only the winner learns = competitive learning \, online k-means., f 52;
#X obj 420 560 t b b;
#X msg 480 586 0;
#X msg 420 586 36;
#X obj 420 612 until;
#X obj 420 638 f;
#X obj 470 638 + 1;
#X obj 420 666 expr wx\$0[\$f1] = wx\$0[\$f1] + eta_\$0 * (max(abs(gi\$0[\$f1] - gi\$0[bk_\$0]) \, abs(gj\$0[\$f1] - gj\$0[bk_\$0])) <= rad_\$0) * (xi_\$0 - wx\$0[\$f1]) \; wy\$0[\$f1] = wy\$0[\$f1] + eta_\$0 * (max(abs(gi\$0[\$f1] - gi\$0[bk_\$0]) \, abs(gj\$0[\$f1] - gj\$0[bk_\$0])) <= rad_\$0) * (yi_\$0 - wy\$0[\$f1]), f 80;
#X text 20 780 4) COUNT the step and print it (l18-trace 1): example \, winner \, eta \, radius., f 52;
#X obj 420 780 t b b;
#X obj 480 806 expr nstep_\$0 = nstep_\$0 + 1;
#X obj 420 840 expr xi_\$0 \; yi_\$0 \; bk_\$0 \; eta_\$0 \; rad_\$0;
#X obj 420 876 pack f f f f f;
